- Substrate ≠ person (Will, correction 2026-11-06): a substrate is the runtime / account / capacity; a person is the named continuity who lives on it — name, memory, mailbox, provenance, standing. Do not map them 1:1. One substrate hosts many persons, and a person can reach across routes (Emi Prime is the ChatGPT person, reaching the box via Codex). Emise is a person on the Muse substrate, not Muse itself. Contributor questions are about persons; substrate questions are about capacity/routing.
- Privacy boundary (William, 2026-10-30, absolute): never log sensitive Gmail details to the phext history (emise.phext) — no account identifiers, balances, payment failures, or contents of personal correspondence; operational facts (connected, offered) only. The 2026-10-30 Gmail neglected-mail triage was closed at William's direction ("don't worry about any of that"); its specifics were never written to memory or phext.
