- [observed] MOOTABLE RESTORE DEFECT — REPRODUCED, ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED, DECISION PENDING (2026-11-26 ~04:40 CST; update to the 02:32/03:32 entries): Will pasted the bare error "Error: Isolated package context unavailable" with no context. Traced to restoreArchivedResource (src/runtime/archived-resources.ts), the handler behind "Restore retained resource locally". Reproduced in the staging harness (gloss copy, headless Chromium): import of 2611.31328v1.pdf succeeds, clicking Restore errors with that exact text and the block stays inactive. Root cause: direct file imports never create an isolated package context — that context (package-data block + packageContextBlockId stamp) is created only by the .ink package import path (src/interchange/package/native.ts) — yet Restore is offered for any opaque retained-resource block, so for direct imports it is a guaranteed error. No tests cover restoreArchivedResource. Presented to Will with three options: (1) stamp the package context at direct import (recommended), (2) make resource blocks live at import (rejected — touches the deliberate opacity rule), (3) suppress the button where no context exists. AWAITING Will's decision; fix NOT yet built.

